      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that Brya followed suit after Volteer. Volteer needed CONFIG_BYPASS_CBI_EEPROM during development because the CBI WP was decoupled. Speaking with the Brya EE folks, it sounded like they were doing the same as Volteer. Therefore, I don\u0027t see why this check needs to be removed?\n\n* You should bypass the WP check if the WPs are decoupled.\n* If the EC does not control the EEPROM CBI WP, then you can only bypass the check with CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED. This represents the development phase.",
      "revId": "2cdba6805da0816d5ded090855fa037cf6552027",
